# Environment of the sniffarr service; see https://sarak.sh/mikluko/sniffarr/src/branch/main/docs/configuration.md.

# The components of the one process: the API with the database, the web UI,
# the DHT sniffer and the metadata fetcher, with the DHT port forwarded by
# UPnP. Every flag is listed under "Configuration" in the README.
SNIFFARR_FLAGS=-api -ui -sniff -fetch -upnp

# The database is /var/lib/sniffarr/sniffarr.db; SNIFFARR_DB in the unit.

# Without a TypeSafe key, only the rules classify.
#TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# The web UI listens on :8081 and authenticates nobody: put a proxy in front
# of it, or bind it to loopback.
#SNIFFARR_UI_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8081

# Keys of the Torznab indexer and of the Radarr and Sonarr webhook; each is
# served only when its key is set.
#SNIFFARR_TORZNAB_TOKEN=
#SNIFFARR_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=

# Audio languages tracked as dubs, BCP-47 tags.
#SNIFFARR_AUDIO_LANGUAGES=ru
